1
00:00:05,262 --> 00:00:08,627
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Makkan Period,

2
00:00:09,143 --> 00:00:10,723
by Imam Anwar Al-Awlaki,

3
00:00:11,794 --> 00:00:12,725
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:12,764 --> 00:00:17,137
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

5
00:00:18,285 --> 00:00:20,337
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

6
00:00:21,484 --> 00:00:26,782
Few months after, the end of the embargo.

7
00:00:28,597 --> 00:00:29,989
About six months later

8
00:00:31,811 --> 00:00:38,014
 the man who has supported the Messenger of Allah ﷺ

9
00:00:40,215 --> 00:00:45,365
was now, on his deathbed leaving this world.

10
00:00:47,034 --> 00:00:53,927
Abu Talib(أبو طالب) was dying and Muhammadﷺ was on his side

11
00:00:54,855 --> 00:01:01,020
and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told his Uncle, يَا عَمْ O uncle, Say;

12
00:01:01,063 --> 00:01:02,223
 لا اله الا الله

13
00:01:03,504 --> 00:01:11,215
Say that there is no God but Allah, give me this word so that I can witness for you on the Day of Judgment.

14
00:01:13,131 --> 00:01:17,606
Give me something in my hand so that I could argue on your behalf on the Day of Judgment.

15
00:01:19,611 --> 00:01:21,050
All what I want from you is to say;

16
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:22,368
لا اله الا الله

17
00:01:24,348 --> 00:01:26,518
Sitting on the other side, was who?

18
00:01:27,764 --> 00:01:28,775
 Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

19
00:01:30,276 --> 00:01:35,283
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), it's amazing, wherever you go in Seerah(سيرة), you would find this man in front of you,

20
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:41,391
causing problems leading in evil.

21
00:01:41,582 --> 00:01:46,337
Wherever you go in Seerah(سيرة), you'll just have Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) standing right there in front of you.

22
00:01:48,681 --> 00:01:57,372
He was relentless in his efforts to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ, he did not give up until the last moment.

23
00:01:59,847 --> 00:02:03,264
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) and Abdullah Bin Abi Umayyah(عبدالله بن ابي امية) were sitting on the other side.

24
00:02:03,304 --> 00:02:05,153
 Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) interjected and said,

25
00:02:05,749 --> 00:02:09,301
O Ibn Abdul Muttalib(ابن عبدالمطلب) are you going to die

26
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:13,019
on a religion other than the religion of Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب)?

27
00:02:13,601 --> 00:02:17,756
Are you going to denounce the religion of your father?

28
00:02:19,652 --> 00:02:22,223
Rasool Allah ﷺ repeated again.

29
00:02:23,136 --> 00:02:24,240
O my uncle say;

30
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,272
 لا اله الا الله

31
00:02:26,868 --> 00:02:31,005
And Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) continued interrupting

32
00:02:32,356 --> 00:02:38,909
and then it went on until about Abu Talib(ابو طالب) pronounced his last words. He said:

33
00:02:39,054 --> 00:02:41,109
بَلْ عَلَى مِلَّة عَبْدَ الْمُطَّلِبْ

34
00:02:41,672 --> 00:02:44,981
I am dying on the religion of my father, Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب).

35
00:02:45,727 --> 00:02:47,525
Those were his last words.

36
00:02:48,942 --> 00:02:53,255
This narration by the way that I mentioned to you is in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ), there's another narration in Muslim(مسلم).

37
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:56,569
Let's first finish this narration of Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ).

38
00:02:57,878 --> 00:02:59,533
So, Abu Talib(أبو طالب) passed away.

39
00:03:00,490 --> 00:03:03,305
The Messenger of Allah, Muhammadﷺ said:

40
00:03:04,005 --> 00:03:07,226
I'm going to continue asking Allah to forgive him.

41
00:03:07,926 --> 00:03:10,008
Unless I'm provident from doing so.

42
00:03:10,804 --> 00:03:14,170
I'm going to keep on asking Allah to forgive my uncle.

43
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,833
You know, that was a very, very difficult moment on Rasool Allah ﷺ.

44
00:03:18,873 --> 00:03:24,840
Remember Abu Talib(أبوطالب) was the one, who raised up Muhammadﷺ,

45
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:28,034
he sponsored him, he took care of him at the age of eight.

46
00:03:29,728 --> 00:03:33,396
So, he was the one caring for him, in his childhood

47
00:03:34,058 --> 00:03:38,262
and then he's the one who stood beside him in his adulthood.

48
00:03:39,924 --> 00:03:47,535
And Abu Talib(ابو طالب) was supporting, defending, protecting Muhammadﷺ for over 42 years.

49
00:03:48,973 --> 00:03:50,978
It started at the age of eight,

50
00:03:51,601 --> 00:03:55,340
and it went on, until Rasool Allah ﷺ was at the age of 50.

51
00:03:56,769 --> 00:04:05,748
So, we can say that Abu Talib(ابو طالب) has spent most of his time in defense of Muhammadﷺ.

52
00:04:06,325 --> 00:04:15,058
So, it was an extremely difficult time for Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه to see that his dear uncle is dying as a disbelievers.

53
00:04:15,098 --> 00:04:17,781
 So, Muhammadﷺ said: I'm gonna ask Allah to forgive him.

54
00:04:18,731 --> 00:04:22,344
And he asked Allah to forgive him, until Allah revealed the verse.

55
00:04:23,484 --> 00:04:32,700
مَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِيِّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوا لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ وَلَوْ

56
00:04:32,985 --> 00:04:43,466
وَلَوْ كَانُوا أُولِي قُرْبَىٰ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ أَنَّهُمْ أَصْحَابُ الْجَحِيمِ۝

57
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:51,853
It is not fitting for the Prophet and those who believe that they should invoke Allah for forgiveness for pagans,

58
00:04:52,151 --> 00:04:58,592
even though they be of kin, after it has become clear to them, that they are companions of the Fire.

59
00:05:00,083 --> 00:05:06,635
It is not allowed for you to seek forgiveness for somebody who died on disbelief.

60
00:05:07,806 --> 00:05:10,951
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was forbidden from doing that.

61
00:05:12,121 --> 00:05:17,250
In this narration by Muslim(مسلم), Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling his uncle to say;

62
00:05:17,290 --> 00:05:18,361
 لا اله الا الله

63
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,381
His uncle responded by saying

64
00:05:20,421 --> 00:05:26,495
if it were not for Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), insulting me and saying that it was only fear of death that made me say it,

65
00:05:26,886 --> 00:05:29,081
I would do so and please you.

66
00:05:29,894 --> 00:05:32,465
Abu Talib(ابو طالب) knew that it would please Muhammadﷺ,

67
00:05:32,505 --> 00:05:39,063
he knew how much it would hurt the Messenger of Allah to know that his uncle died as disbelievers.

68
00:05:39,381 --> 00:05:44,663
So, Abu Talib(ابو طالب), Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), he was even sympathetic to Muhammadﷺ in this case.

69
00:05:45,159 --> 00:05:47,394
He said I would have said it, just to please you,

70
00:05:47,771 --> 00:05:50,849
but I don't want the news to get out to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

71
00:05:51,095 --> 00:05:53,125
that I did it out of fear of dying.

72
00:05:54,296 --> 00:05:57,096
So, it was a matter of honor and dignity for him.

73
00:05:57,573 --> 00:06:01,265
Not to say it, and that's when Allahسبحانه وتعالى revealed the verse,

74
00:06:01,348 --> 00:06:04,797
إِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ ۚ

75
00:06:05,583 --> 00:06:08,220
You cannot give guidance to those, whom you love,

76
00:06:08,756 --> 00:06:11,923
but it is Allah Who gives guidance to the ones He wills.

77
00:06:13,116 --> 00:06:16,891
So, guidance is not in the hands of anyone except Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

78
00:06:17,188 --> 00:06:22,109
even the Prophet of Allah, his mission is to convey the message and not to convert,

79
00:06:23,399 --> 00:06:29,100
converting the heart of a person is in the hands of Allah, not in the hands of people.

80
00:06:29,775 --> 00:06:35,142
And therefore in Islam coercion in faith is not allowed,

81
00:06:35,452 --> 00:06:36,530
لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ ۖ

82
00:06:36,889 --> 00:06:39,256
There's no coercion in religion,

83
00:06:39,562 --> 00:06:42,349
because this is something beyond our ability,

84
00:06:42,705 --> 00:06:45,779
you cannot coerce something on the heart of a person.

85
00:06:46,061 --> 00:06:52,704
So, it should be a matter of choice by people they have the freedom to choose their faith.

86
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:56,153
And that is how they would be held accountable in front of Allahسبحانه وتعالى,

87
00:06:56,193 --> 00:06:58,007
it is because of that freedom that they have.

88
00:06:58,572 --> 00:07:04,889
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ is dealing with this tragic event that happened to him,

89
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:10,016
two months later, Khadijahرضي الله عنها dies.

90
00:07:12,546 --> 00:07:16,487
Rasool Allah ﷺ is still dealing with the death of his Uncle

91
00:07:16,527 --> 00:07:21,449
and here his dear wife, the most beloved person to him, passes away.

92
00:07:22,508 --> 00:07:27,270
This year was called Aam-El-Huzn(عام الحزن), the year of sorrow.

93
00:07:27,806 --> 00:07:32,737
And this was the 10th year after Rasool Allah ﷺ received revelation.

94
00:07:33,669 --> 00:07:37,164
It was the most tragic time on Muhammadﷺ

95
00:07:37,394 --> 00:07:43,564
because he lost the most two influential persons in supporting his message.

96
00:07:43,654 --> 00:07:48,193
Khadijahرضي الله عنها, who offered Rasool Allah ﷺ with psychological support,

97
00:07:48,481 --> 00:07:51,299
in addition to financial support due to her business

98
00:07:51,824 --> 00:07:55,328
and Abu Talib(ابو طالب), who offered Muhammadﷺ with physical support.

99
00:07:55,983 --> 00:08:00,549
So, suddenly these two pillars which he was standing on, collapsed.

100
00:08:02,473 --> 00:08:06,885
So, this year is not called the year of tragedy, the year of sorrow,

101
00:08:07,147 --> 00:08:10,266
just because Rasool Allah ﷺ lost two dear people,

102
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:15,834
but also because it was such a setback to the preaching of the message.

103
00:08:16,866 --> 00:08:22,029
Rasool Allah ﷺ, who had freedom in going around preaching the message

104
00:08:22,453 --> 00:08:26,697
was now being blocked because his uncle passed away.

105
00:08:27,166 --> 00:08:33,761
And Rasool Allah ﷺ, who would go home to find comfort with his wife Khadijah(خديجه), would go home and find no one.

106
00:08:34,118 --> 00:08:38,803
Rasool Allah ﷺ remained for about two or three years, unmarried.

107
00:08:41,439 --> 00:08:44,904
So, it was a very difficult time on Muhammadﷺ.

108
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:53,864
Some scholars would say that there was wisdom in this happening, in the same time

109
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:58,327
 and that is to increase the dependence of the Muslims on Allah.

110
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:04,264
So, rather than the message being protected by Abu Talib(ابو طالب),

111
00:09:04,839 --> 00:09:06,930
and supported by Khadijah(خديجه),

112
00:09:07,335 --> 00:09:11,598
now there would be more reliance on Allahسبحانه وتعالى, because there was no one else

113
00:09:12,848 --> 00:09:16,459
no one around Rasool Allah ﷺ to give him that same support.

114
00:09:17,054 --> 00:09:22,345
So, this would increase the Tawakkal(توكل) the trust that the Muslims have in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

115
00:09:22,385 --> 00:09:25,350
 This is a comment that was given by some of the scholars.

116
00:09:27,077 --> 00:09:33,391
Allahسبحانه وتعالى revealed the Surah(سورة) called Al-Ish'rah(اِلشْرَح).

117
00:09:34,879 --> 00:09:36,677
And in that Surah(سورة), it says;

118
00:09:37,389 --> 00:09:39,353
فَإِنَّ مَعَ الْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا۝

119
00:09:40,624 --> 00:09:43,403
With difficulty comes ease.

120
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:50,053
Rasool Allah ﷺ went through this most tragic time in his life.

121
00:09:50,787 --> 00:09:57,460
So, it was followed with one of the best blessings given to him by Allah.

122
00:09:58,607 --> 00:10:04,931
Because of the size of the calamity, the bounty that followed it, was great.

123
00:10:06,757 --> 00:10:12,149
Rasool Allah ﷺ narrates and this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) similar narrations are in Muslim(مسلم)

124
00:10:12,204 --> 00:10:17,015
 and in Masnad Imam Ahmad(مسند امام أحمد) in most of the books of Hadith(حديث), these narrations exist.

125
00:10:17,823 --> 00:10:20,011
Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

126
00:10:20,238 --> 00:10:24,322
while I was in Al-Hateem(ألحطيم) or Al-Hijr(ألحجر)

127
00:10:25,050 --> 00:10:32,020
and this is the semi circle area close to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), which is part of the original building of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

128
00:10:32,354 --> 00:10:34,541
Rasool Allah ﷺ said that he was there at night.

129
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,555
The Messenger of Allah said,

130
00:10:37,952 --> 00:10:46,082
I received a visitor, an angel, who came and opened my abdomen and pulled out my heart.

131
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:54,514
And then my heart was placed in a basin, golden basin, filled with faith, Eeman(ايمان).

132
00:10:55,554 --> 00:11:01,216
And my heart was placed in it and washed and then stuffed and replaced.

133
00:11:02,866 --> 00:11:05,136
And then I was presented an animal,

134
00:11:06,025 --> 00:11:10,479
smaller than a horse, larger than a donkey.

135
00:11:12,049 --> 00:11:14,438
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) was narrating this Hadith(حديث).

136
00:11:14,990 --> 00:11:17,458
And his students one of At-Tabaeen(ألتابعين), Al-Jarood(الجرود),

137
00:11:17,538 --> 00:11:19,906
asked Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك), Is this animal Al-Buraak(ألبراق).?

138
00:11:20,104 --> 00:11:21,580
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) said: Yes.

139
00:11:23,105 --> 00:11:30,829
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This animal would take a stride as far as it can see.

140
00:11:32,249 --> 00:11:39,441
So, the Messenger of Allah is trying to describe to us the speed of this animal.

141
00:11:40,288 --> 00:11:49,376
And Rasool Ullah described it as that this animal would place its hoofs at the extent of its sight,

142
00:11:49,487 --> 00:11:53,016
 it would take a stride as far as it can see, with one leap

143
00:11:53,512 --> 00:12:00,769
it would wrap the distance equivalent to the distance you could see or look forward.

144
00:12:01,666 --> 00:12:06,755
So, it was an extremely fast beast very fast, swift.

145
00:12:07,347 --> 00:12:09,745
You just see the earth wrapping in front of you.

146
00:12:11,769 --> 00:12:16,553
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) told me to mount this animal and then he would guide me.

147
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:22,227
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, in another Hadith(حديث) that I was taken to

148
00:12:22,417 --> 00:12:26,925
and this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim(مسلم), this portion was not mentioned in the Hadith(حديث) of Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ),

149
00:12:26,955 --> 00:12:30,046
you have bits and pieces of Al-Isra wal Miraj(ألإسراء و المعراج) mentioned in different Ahadith(احاديث)

150
00:12:30,366 --> 00:12:34,221
in Muslim(مسلم) it says that Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) took me to Jerusalem.

151
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:39,844
And I tied my mount at the gates of Al-Masjid(مسجد)

152
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,391
and then I entered and prayed two Rakah(ركعة).

153
00:12:44,403 --> 00:12:47,716
And it states that Rasool Allah ﷺ was an Imam(امام),

154
00:12:48,648 --> 00:12:52,301
and the people who were following him were the Prophets.

155
00:12:54,441 --> 00:12:56,164
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

156
00:12:56,660 --> 00:13:00,970
I was led by Jibreel(جبريل) up in the heavens.

157
00:13:01,585 --> 00:13:06,965
He said, we made it all the way to the gates of the lowest heaven, the nearest heaven.

158
00:13:08,076 --> 00:13:09,713
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) knocked on the gates.

159
00:13:10,189 --> 00:13:14,080
So, the gatekeepers said: Who is it?

160
00:13:14,829 --> 00:13:16,565
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said, it is Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل).

161
00:13:17,418 --> 00:13:18,458
And who was with you.?

162
00:13:18,545 --> 00:13:19,458
 Muhammad(محمد).

163
00:13:19,914 --> 00:13:22,235
Was he given, his mission?

164
00:13:22,664 --> 00:13:23,960
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said: Yes.

165
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:29,039
They responded by saying, he is welcome, and his arrival is a pleasure.

166
00:13:29,611 --> 00:13:31,015
And they opened the gates

167
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:37,442
So, you can see no one can make it through unless, they have permission, they have clearance.

168
00:13:37,937 --> 00:13:41,996
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) being the angel of Allah, who was going up and down the heavens with Al-Wahee(ألوحي),

169
00:13:42,498 --> 00:13:44,556
he told them, I am Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) so he can go through,

170
00:13:44,691 --> 00:13:46,667
who's with you.? Muhammadﷺ!

171
00:13:46,975 --> 00:13:48,872
Was he already given the mission.?

172
00:13:49,008 --> 00:13:52,112
So, they didn't know yet that Muhammadﷺ was already a Prophet,

173
00:13:52,151 --> 00:13:57,285
when they were informed, immediately they opened the gates and said, he is welcome.

174
00:13:57,647 --> 00:13:59,527
And his arrival is a pleasure,

175
00:13:59,785 --> 00:14:01,109
We're happy that he's here.

176
00:14:01,588 --> 00:14:10,043
They opened the gates Rasool Allah ﷺ said, I went in and I found there in my father Adamعليه السّلام,

177
00:14:11,293 --> 00:14:15,779
the Messenger of Allah said Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) introduced me to Adam(آدم) and said,

178
00:14:16,007 --> 00:14:19,144
this is your father Adam(آدم). Greet him.!

179
00:14:20,563 --> 00:14:22,937
So, I said, Assalam-O-Alaikum(اسلام عليكم).

180
00:14:23,473 --> 00:14:28,602
Adam(آدم) saluted me in return and said, Walaikum Salam(وعليكم السلام)

181
00:14:29,336 --> 00:14:36,957
and then Adamعليه السّلام said, welcome to my pure son. Welcome to the pure Prophet.

182
00:14:38,862 --> 00:14:40,834
When I think of this meeting,

183
00:14:41,607 --> 00:14:47,297
I try to imagine the pleasure and happiness that both the Prophets had.

184
00:14:48,011 --> 00:14:55,725
You know, Imagine Adamعليه السّلام is meeting the brightest and greatest of his children, Muhammadﷺ.

185
00:14:55,765 --> 00:15:01,193
 He is meeting him for the first time, after thousands of years.

186
00:15:01,868 --> 00:15:05,233
Now Adamعليه السّلام has a chance to meet his greatest son.

187
00:15:06,186 --> 00:15:10,173
And imagine the surprise of Muhammadﷺ to meet his father Adam(آدم),

188
00:15:10,213 --> 00:15:12,923
I mean imagine you have Adam(آدم) in front of you and you greeting him.

189
00:15:13,609 --> 00:15:16,149
It must have been such a pleasurable moment

190
00:15:16,762 --> 00:15:21,900
and they might have wished to sit down together and have a conversation.

191
00:15:22,203 --> 00:15:28,443
But remember that Muhammadﷺ in this journey is on a tight schedule, he has a lot waiting ahead of him.

192
00:15:30,556 --> 00:15:36,404
So, Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) carried Muhammadﷺ, and they went up to the gates of the second heaven.

193
00:15:38,031 --> 00:15:42,006
They knocked same thing, they were asked Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), who is with you.?

194
00:15:42,046 --> 00:15:43,921
Muhammadﷺ! Is he a Nabi(نبي).?

195
00:15:44,133 --> 00:15:45,791
Has he been given a Risalah(رسالة)?

196
00:15:45,982 --> 00:15:53,109
They opened the gates, Muhammadﷺ said: I went in and I met Jesus and John, the two cousins,

197
00:15:53,945 --> 00:15:55,292
Eesa(عيسى) and Yahya(يحيى).

198
00:15:55,633 --> 00:15:59,990
Yahya(يحيى) is referred to, in the Christian literature as John the Baptist.

199
00:16:00,816 --> 00:16:02,022
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

200
00:16:02,245 --> 00:16:07,348
And I exchanged greetings with them and what are the greetings of Islam, and the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)?

201
00:16:07,372 --> 00:16:10,724
Assalam-O-Alaikum(ألسلام عليكم), Peace be upon you, that's the greeting.

202
00:16:11,536 --> 00:16:16,729
And then we moved ahead to the third heaven,

203
00:16:18,316 --> 00:16:25,069
knocked on the gates, went through and I met with Joseph, Yusufعليه السّلام.

204
00:16:25,316 --> 00:16:26,722
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

205
00:16:26,972 --> 00:16:29,328
وَاِذَا بِهِ اُوْتِيَ شَطْرَ الْحُسْن

206
00:16:29,651 --> 00:16:31,859
He has been given half of beauty.

207
00:16:32,297 --> 00:16:37,478
So, if you had the big block of beauty half of it was with Yusufعليه السّلام

208
00:16:38,847 --> 00:16:45,343
We made it to the forth heaven, went through and I met with Idrisعليه السّلام

209
00:16:45,850 --> 00:16:46,757
 and Allahسبحانه وتعالى says;

210
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,478
وَرَفَعْنَاهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا

211
00:16:48,545 --> 00:16:52,383
We have elevated him to a very high status, he was in the fourth heaven.

212
00:16:54,117 --> 00:17:01,015
We went to the fifth heaven and therein, I met with Haroon(هارون), Aaron, peace be upon him.

213
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:07,029
And then I went to the sixth heaven and I met Musaعليه السّلام,

214
00:17:08,239 --> 00:17:12,676
and his meeting with Musa(موسى) was an eventful meetings, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

215
00:17:13,292 --> 00:17:15,739
always Musa(موسى) is surrounded with important events,

216
00:17:16,672 --> 00:17:18,949
in Qur'an, one of the scholars said,

217
00:17:19,024 --> 00:17:20,754
كَادَ الْقُرْآنُ اَنْ يَكُوْنَ مُوْسَى

218
00:17:21,092 --> 00:17:23,832
Qur'an was almost going to be the story of Musa(موسى),

219
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:26,470
he's mentioned, so frequently therein

220
00:17:26,915 --> 00:17:30,400
and his personality is so outstanding

221
00:17:30,935 --> 00:17:36,406
Whenever the name of Musaعليه السّلام is mentioned there's something important going to happen.

222
00:17:37,756 --> 00:17:40,526
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed by Musa(موسى),

223
00:17:40,748 --> 00:17:46,837
Musa(موسى) started to weep after they greeted each other, and Musa(موسى) welcomed Muhammadﷺ.

224
00:17:47,945 --> 00:17:49,455
Musa(موسى) started to weep,

225
00:17:49,737 --> 00:17:51,997
when he was asked, How come you're weeping. He said,

226
00:17:52,022 --> 00:17:55,792
غُلَامٌ بُعِثَ بَعْدِيْ يدخل مِنْ أمته اَلْجَنَّةْ اَكْثَرُ مِنْ اُمَّتِيْ

227
00:17:56,188 --> 00:17:59,832
 A young man was given Prophet hood after me,

228
00:18:00,214 --> 00:18:04,132
and he will have more of his followers entering paradise than mine.

229
00:18:06,077 --> 00:18:12,572
Up until, that moment, Musa(موسى) had the largest following of any Prophet.

230
00:18:13,326 --> 00:18:19,160
The children of Israel(اسرائيل) were the largest believing nation up until that point,

231
00:18:19,854 --> 00:18:21,769
but now there was a new world record,

232
00:18:22,344 --> 00:18:24,331
by the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

233
00:18:24,827 --> 00:18:27,091
So, Musa(موسى) wept, he cried,

234
00:18:27,766 --> 00:18:31,877
and you can see that there is competition between the Prophets, ﷺ

235
00:18:32,227 --> 00:18:36,568
but you will notice that it's not the competition of jealousy and envy.

236
00:18:36,608 --> 00:18:38,326
 It's a compassionate competition.

237
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:44,636
And you'll see that in the upcoming conversation between Muhammadﷺ and Musaعليه السّلام.

238
00:18:46,421 --> 00:18:51,434
Rasool Allah ﷺ said and I moved up to the seventh heaven

239
00:18:51,936 --> 00:18:57,764
and I went in and I met my father Ibrahim عليه السّلام and I exchanged Salaam(سلام) with him.

240
00:18:59,236 --> 00:19:03,329
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, and then I was presented with Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور).

241
00:19:04,361 --> 00:19:10,487
And in one narration, it states that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) actually had his back, kneeling towards Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور).

242
00:19:10,725 --> 00:19:12,026
What is Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور).?

243
00:19:12,645 --> 00:19:14,830
Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور) has been mentioned in Qur'an.

244
00:19:15,008 --> 00:19:15,689
وَالطُّورِ۝

245
00:19:15,879 --> 00:19:17,032
وَكِتَابٍ مَسْطُورٍ۝

246
00:19:17,363 --> 00:19:18,466
فِي رَقٍّ مَنْشُورٍ۝

247
00:19:18,593 --> 00:19:19,978
وَالْبَيْتِ الْمَعْمُورِ۝

248
00:19:20,875 --> 00:19:27,290
Allahسبحانه وتعالى is making an oath in the established house; Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور),

249
00:19:27,952 --> 00:19:35,789
Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور) to the creation of the heavens is equivalent to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) to us.

250
00:19:37,853 --> 00:19:41,878
Just as we make the Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

251
00:19:43,088 --> 00:19:47,066
and it is the first house on earth established for the worship of Allah.

252
00:19:47,328 --> 00:19:50,129
The same thing is to be said about Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور).

253
00:19:50,278 --> 00:19:55,789
So, as Muslims will visit Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), Angels will visit Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور).

254
00:19:57,198 --> 00:20:06,815
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور) is visited by 70,000 angels every day,

255
00:20:07,148 --> 00:20:09,383
and they never come back to it again.

256
00:20:12,030 --> 00:20:13,943
Do you understand the implications of that?

257
00:20:15,539 --> 00:20:23,729
When Rasool Allah ﷺ says that every day a new group of 70,000 angels would visit the established house.

258
00:20:24,912 --> 00:20:26,464
 How many angels are there?

259
00:20:27,793 --> 00:20:32,612
If on a daily basis, you have 70,000 Angels visiting it and they never come back again.

260
00:20:34,179 --> 00:20:35,563
How many angels are there?

261
00:20:36,575 --> 00:20:39,125
And for how long has this been going on?

262
00:20:39,819 --> 00:20:43,815
For how many thousands or millions or billions of years?

263
00:20:44,688 --> 00:20:47,885
So, you multiply all of those days by 70,000.

264
00:20:48,710 --> 00:20:50,266
How many angels are there.

265
00:20:52,196 --> 00:20:54,020
It puts us human beings to shame.

266
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:59,036
I mean, we're saying that we have over population on the Earth 6 billion of us.

267
00:20:59,866 --> 00:21:04,203
Who are we compared to the world of the angels this massive creation.!

268
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:07,394
You know, Rasool Allahﷺ says;

269
00:21:07,458 --> 00:21:09,755
أَطَّتِ السَّماءُ، وحُقَّ لها أن تَئِطَّ

270
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:13,832
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; the heavens above you are moaning

271
00:21:14,371 --> 00:21:22,000
and they are justified to moan because on every space equivalent to the size of four fingers,

272
00:21:22,557 --> 00:21:26,071
there is an angel bowing down in Rakoh(ركوع)

273
00:21:26,778 --> 00:21:30,251
or prostrating in Sujood(سجود), worshipping Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

274
00:21:32,091 --> 00:21:33,892
all over the heavens above us.

275
00:21:34,923 --> 00:21:42,547
Every position every area or volume equivalent to the size of four fingers is occupied by an angel, worshiping Allah.

276
00:21:43,946 --> 00:21:47,250
So, this is a vast, huge creation

277
00:21:48,024 --> 00:21:51,875
that makes us the world of the human beings seem insignificant.

278
00:21:54,194 --> 00:21:55,436
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

279
00:21:55,531 --> 00:21:56,566
And by the way

280
00:21:57,693 --> 00:22:04,155
in the narration that states that Ibrahimعليه السّلام was kneeling towards Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور).

281
00:22:05,159 --> 00:22:15,456
It is symbolic to have Ibrahim عليه السّلام in that position after he passed away, sitting next to Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور)

282
00:22:15,829 --> 00:22:18,232
because he was the one who built Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) on Earth.

283
00:22:19,085 --> 00:22:21,065
So, when Allah took his soul away.

284
00:22:21,406 --> 00:22:26,613
Allahسبحانه وتعالى had him rest next to Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور), the house of the angels.

285
00:22:28,795 --> 00:22:32,418
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I saw Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهی).

286
00:22:33,034 --> 00:22:37,416
I traveled further, and I reached to Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهی)

287
00:22:38,448 --> 00:22:43,036
Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهى) is a loat tree, it's a tree.

288
00:22:43,532 --> 00:22:46,290
But it is Al-Muntaha(المنتهى), Al-Muntaha(المنتهى) is the end.

289
00:22:46,925 --> 00:22:50,073
So, it's the end of the heavens.

290
00:22:50,668 --> 00:22:54,470
Beyond that you get into the world of the afterlife, you have paradise,

291
00:22:54,866 --> 00:22:57,650
you have the throne of Allah, you have Al- Kursi(ألكرسي)

292
00:22:57,969 --> 00:23:02,902
So, Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهى) is the end of this universe created by Allahسبحانه وتعالى,

293
00:23:02,942 --> 00:23:07,480
you have seven heavens one over the other.

294
00:23:07,882 --> 00:23:13,134
And then after that, you have Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهى), and then you get beyond that into different world.

295
00:23:13,643 --> 00:23:19,789
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ reached to that Sidra(سدره) and Rasool Ullah saw four Rivers emanating from it.

296
00:23:20,881 --> 00:23:23,333
And he asked Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), what are these four rivers.?

297
00:23:23,425 --> 00:23:27,198
So, he was told, two of them are apparent and two of them are hidden.

298
00:23:27,508 --> 00:23:30,492
The apparent ones are the Nile and Euphrates

299
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,532
and the hidden ones are the two rivers of paradise.

300
00:23:34,653 --> 00:23:37,208
What it means by the Nile and the Euphrates?

301
00:23:37,565 --> 00:23:44,225
Is that because these rivers are so blessed in this world, there is an equivalent of them up there.

302
00:23:45,999 --> 00:23:53,055
And that tree is so close to paradise that you have two rivers of Paradise passing, from under it.

303
00:23:54,246 --> 00:23:58,812
So again, you have the seven heavens one over another.

304
00:23:59,172 --> 00:24:02,603
And then after that you have Al-Bait-Al-Ma'amoor(ألبيت المعمور), which is in the seventh heaven.

305
00:24:02,872 --> 00:24:04,753
 And then after that you have Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهاء).

306
00:24:04,958 --> 00:24:10,732
And then beyond that you get into the world of the paradise and the throne of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

307
00:24:11,074 --> 00:24:13,046
"Now in terms of size,

308
00:24:13,780 --> 00:24:15,881
the lowest heaven which we are in

309
00:24:16,297 --> 00:24:20,655
compared to the heaven above it, is like a ring in a desert.

310
00:24:21,330 --> 00:24:25,246
And the second compared to the third is like a ring in a desert.

311
00:24:25,940 --> 00:24:28,927
And the third to the fourth is like a ring in a desert.

312
00:24:29,209 --> 00:24:32,108
And on and on until we get to the sixth to the seventh.

313
00:24:32,663 --> 00:24:34,378
It's like a ring in a desert.

314
00:24:34,727 --> 00:24:43,010
And then the seventh heaven, compared to the Kursi(كرسي) of Allah, is like a ring in a desert."

315
00:24:45,117 --> 00:24:49,678
Now this lowest heaven that we are living in, in terms of size

316
00:24:50,174 --> 00:24:52,074
we don't even know how vast it is.

317
00:24:52,609 --> 00:24:58,056
All of the known universe today is within the lowest heaven.

318
00:24:59,088 --> 00:25:00,253
Because Allahسبحانه وتعالى says;

319
00:25:00,288 --> 00:25:02,588
وَلَقَدْ زَيَّنَّا السَّمَاءَ الدُّنْيَا بِمَصَابِيحَ

320
00:25:02,850 --> 00:25:05,226
We have adorn the lowest heavens with stars.

321
00:25:05,568 --> 00:25:08,463
So, all of the stars are located within the lowest heaven.

322
00:25:08,822 --> 00:25:14,068
And we haven't even been able to reach to the end of the creation of the stars.

323
00:25:14,465 --> 00:25:19,070
Every now and then we're discovering new galaxies and new clusters and new stars.

324
00:25:20,273 --> 00:25:22,299
So, it is a vast creation.

325
00:25:22,814 --> 00:25:28,581
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had the chance to go through all of it, on that amazing journey.

326
00:25:29,752 --> 00:25:34,264
After Rasool Allah ﷺ passed the Sidra-Tul-Muntaha(سدرةالمنتهی), this tree.

327
00:25:35,752 --> 00:25:37,761
He went further, up

328
00:25:39,963 --> 00:25:44,742
and he made it all the way until he met with Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

329
00:25:46,464 --> 00:25:50,117
And that was the combination of this trip,

330
00:25:51,293 --> 00:25:59,204
he reaches to the heights and he speaks to Allahعَزّوجَلّ, directly.

331
00:26:00,136 --> 00:26:05,491
Allahسبحانه وتعالى prescribed on Muhammadﷺ Fifty(50) daily prayers.

332
00:26:08,450 --> 00:26:10,050
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

333
00:26:10,637 --> 00:26:19,298
I descended and on my way back, I pass by Moses, Musaعليه السّلام,

334
00:26:20,392 --> 00:26:24,080
who asked me, what did Allah tell you?

335
00:26:25,330 --> 00:26:26,301
He said;

336
00:26:26,872 --> 00:26:31,602
Allah has prescribed 50 daily prayers on my nation.

337
00:26:32,838 --> 00:26:38,441
Musa عليه السّلام said: Your people will not be able to handle that.

338
00:26:39,643 --> 00:26:47,147
I have tested people before you and I have experienced the children of Israel for a very long time.

339
00:26:47,453 --> 00:26:50,400
Go back to your Lord and tell him to reduce it.

340
00:26:51,233 --> 00:26:52,540
Tell him to relief you.

341
00:26:53,951 --> 00:26:58,259
Muhammadﷺ followed this advice, senior advice

342
00:26:58,862 --> 00:27:02,165
and he went back to Allahسبحانه وتعالى and told Him,

343
00:27:02,776 --> 00:27:05,982
relief me of some of the prayers.

344
00:27:06,161 --> 00:27:08,406
Allahسبحانه وتعالى reduced them by 10.

345
00:27:09,395 --> 00:27:11,126
Muhammadﷺ went down,

346
00:27:12,308 --> 00:27:13,697
Musa(موسى) said; what happened.?

347
00:27:13,904 --> 00:27:16,034
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, he said, go back.

348
00:27:16,458 --> 00:27:18,462
Ask Allah to give you a further reduction.

349
00:27:19,903 --> 00:27:22,708
Went back again 10 were reduced came down.

350
00:27:22,843 --> 00:27:23,712
What happened?

351
00:27:24,141 --> 00:27:26,494
Allah reduced it to 30, go back again.

352
00:27:28,078 --> 00:27:30,279
Muhammadﷺ goes back another time.

353
00:27:30,494 --> 00:27:32,273
They were reduced from 30 to 20.

354
00:27:32,438 --> 00:27:34,327
Musa(موسى) tells him, go back again.

355
00:27:35,261 --> 00:27:37,589
They were reduced from 20 to 10.

356
00:27:37,883 --> 00:27:40,664
Musa(موسى) told Muhammadﷺ, go back another time.

357
00:27:41,394 --> 00:27:44,479
Muhammadﷺ goes back, it was reduced to five.

358
00:27:44,874 --> 00:27:47,041
He goes down reports it to Musa(موسى),

359
00:27:47,287 --> 00:27:53,333
Musa صلى الله عليه وسلم says; O Muhammad(محمد) I know people,

360
00:27:53,387 --> 00:27:58,035
I have experience, I haven't dealt with the children of Israel(اسرائيل), your nation will not be able to handle it.

361
00:27:58,578 --> 00:28:00,979
Go back and tell Allah to reduce them further.

362
00:28:02,138 --> 00:28:09,087
Muhammadﷺ said: I am so ashamed to go back to Allah and ask him for further reduction.

363
00:28:09,476 --> 00:28:10,333
I cannot.

364
00:28:11,651 --> 00:28:15,153
So, you can see the difference between the personality of Muhammadﷺ and Musa(موسى).

365
00:28:15,670 --> 00:28:18,586
Musa(موسى) wouldn't have minded arguing with Allah further.

366
00:28:20,015 --> 00:28:25,278
Musaعليه السّلام was the one, who asked Allahسبحانه وتعالى, I want to see You.

367
00:28:25,972 --> 00:28:29,571
Allahسبحانه وتعالى has already given Musa(موسى) the favor of speaking to him.

368
00:28:29,754 --> 00:28:31,434
Musa(موسى) wanted more.

369
00:28:31,669 --> 00:28:37,493
Allah I want to see you and then obviously we know what happened, he collapsed.

370
00:28:38,128 --> 00:28:43,036
Musa عليه السّلام is the one, who punched the angel of death and knocked his eye out.

371
00:28:44,643 --> 00:28:49,335
So, Musa عليه السّلام was a very strong man and that was his personality

372
00:28:49,374 --> 00:28:54,187
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah are all the same in their Da'wah(دعوة) but their personalities are different.

373
00:28:56,342 --> 00:28:58,394
So, Muhammadﷺ did not go back

374
00:28:58,513 --> 00:29:05,610
and he heard a voice saying that this is the prescription on you five daily prayers,

375
00:29:05,951 --> 00:29:08,125
but you will receive the reward of 50.

376
00:29:10,325 --> 00:29:17,235
Rasool Allah ﷺ made it back to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), on the same night.

377
00:29:19,159 --> 00:29:24,663
Rasool Allahﷺ went to Umm Aimen(أم أيمن) and he told her about what happened.

378
00:29:24,703 --> 00:29:28,187
 He said, I've been to Jerusalem and back, in this night.

379
00:29:29,053 --> 00:29:33,678
She said: O Messenger of Allah, do not tell anyone about that,

380
00:29:35,325 --> 00:29:36,923
nobody will believe it.

381
00:29:38,034 --> 00:29:39,044
It's impossible,

382
00:29:40,700 --> 00:29:42,314
now Umm Aimen(أم أيمن) believed it

383
00:29:43,227 --> 00:29:45,352
but she said that the people will not.

384
00:29:45,987 --> 00:29:47,899
The Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) will not.

385
00:29:49,209 --> 00:29:52,364
The journey towards Jerusalem used to take one month,

386
00:29:53,672 --> 00:29:55,813
Rasool Allah ﷺ made it, within one night,

387
00:29:56,298 --> 00:30:03,207
not only to Jerusalem but to Jerusalem back and he also went all the way to meet with Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

388
00:30:04,772 --> 00:30:09,338
Umm Aimenرضي الله عنها told him, do not tell your people about it.

389
00:30:10,171 --> 00:30:12,112
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I will,

390
00:30:13,207 --> 00:30:18,464
I will convey the message, regardless of what the people will say.

391
00:30:18,908 --> 00:30:21,392
It's part of my mission I will tell them what happened.

392
00:30:22,265 --> 00:30:23,830
وَمَا عَلَيْنَا إِلَّا الْبَلَاغُ الْمُبِينُ

393
00:30:23,855 --> 00:30:25,906
Your responsibility is to convey.

394
00:30:26,297 --> 00:30:33,518
Rasool Allah ﷺ obviously realized the weight of this news and how difficult it will be.

395
00:30:33,558 --> 00:30:38,708
So, he went out and was quiet and somber.

396
00:30:39,690 --> 00:30:44,117
They started to speak to some people and the news reached to Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

397
00:30:44,638 --> 00:30:48,869
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting in the Masjid(مسجد), quiet

398
00:30:49,623 --> 00:30:54,546
and worried about the consequences of this news.

399
00:30:55,657 --> 00:30:56,914
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) heard about it.

400
00:30:56,970 --> 00:31:01,970
He came to Muhammadﷺ and said: O Muhammad, anything new

401
00:31:03,562 --> 00:31:05,442
Muhammadﷺ said: Yes.

402
00:31:06,061 --> 00:31:07,141
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) said: What.?

403
00:31:07,581 --> 00:31:13,591
Muhammadﷺ said: This night, I've visited Jerusalem and came back.

404
00:31:15,072 --> 00:31:16,683
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) said: Jerusalem.

405
00:31:17,551 --> 00:31:19,337
Muhammadﷺ said: Yes.

406
00:31:20,972 --> 00:31:27,931
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) said: O Muhammad(محمد), if I would call your people right now and bring them here.

407
00:31:28,336 --> 00:31:30,929
Would you tell them the same thing you just told me now?

408
00:31:32,026 --> 00:31:34,038
Muhammadﷺ said: Yes, I would.

409
00:31:34,911 --> 00:31:40,685
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) happy and pleased, went running, calling people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

410
00:31:40,725 --> 00:31:45,915
 O people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) come forward and he gathered them and he brought them forth.

411
00:31:46,630 --> 00:31:48,898
And when they're all present he told Muhammadﷺ;

412
00:31:48,938 --> 00:31:53,607
O Muhammad(محمد), can you please tell your people what you just told me a moment ago.

413
00:31:53,896 --> 00:31:56,490
Muhammadﷺ without any hesitation, he said:

414
00:31:57,034 --> 00:32:00,737
I have been to Jerusalem and back, the previous night.

415
00:32:02,304 --> 00:32:09,643
The narrator of the Hadith(حديث) says people started clapping, whistling, laughing they made a big joke out of it.

416
00:32:10,437 --> 00:32:15,352
Imagine the crowds clapping, whistling, laughing and they were falling on each other.

417
00:32:17,336 --> 00:32:22,260
So, some of the seasoned travelers among them, who knew Jerusalem and have been there,

418
00:32:23,033 --> 00:32:27,825
asked Muhammadﷺ to describe the mosque, described Jerusalem to us.?

419
00:32:28,328 --> 00:32:31,546
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I started describing but then I became vexed,

420
00:32:31,689 --> 00:32:36,585
I mean Rasool Allah ﷺ did not spend a long time there to remember every single detail of the place.

421
00:32:37,617 --> 00:32:46,156
But then Muhammadﷺ said: Allah showed me the Masjid(مسجد) the mosque of Jerusalem right in front of my eyes

422
00:32:46,196 --> 00:32:49,447
 and I described it stone by stone, brick by brick.

423
00:32:50,677 --> 00:32:55,786
And they said that he has given an accurate, excellent description.

424
00:32:56,382 --> 00:33:00,711
But then there was something else that was mentioned in another narration by Ibn Is'haq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ).

425
00:33:01,101 --> 00:33:05,089
When Muhammadﷺ was on his way back from Jerusalem to Makkah.

426
00:33:06,300 --> 00:33:10,894
He passed by a caravan belonging to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), at night.

427
00:33:11,295 --> 00:33:13,776
And they have lost the camel of theirs

428
00:33:13,834 --> 00:33:17,144
and Rasool Allah ﷺ because he was up in the air he was able to see it.

429
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:20,493
So, he called them and said that your camel is in this place.

430
00:33:20,580 --> 00:33:22,702
Now they didn't know where the voice is coming from?

431
00:33:23,097 --> 00:33:25,372
And then he drank some of their water.

432
00:33:25,707 --> 00:33:29,192
And he also remember the description of this caravan,

433
00:33:29,650 --> 00:33:31,593
he went back to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he told the people;

434
00:33:32,070 --> 00:33:36,546
and other signs is that, this caravan belonging to you, they lost the camel,

435
00:33:36,871 --> 00:33:40,193
and I gave them directions to it and you can ask them about it.

436
00:33:40,381 --> 00:33:43,731
And also I drank some of their water in such and such container.

437
00:33:44,068 --> 00:33:49,323
And the caravan is headed by a camel and he described the camel, describe the load on the camel.

438
00:33:49,718 --> 00:33:54,696
So, they immediately sent out somebody to go and meet the caravan before it comes into Makkah.

439
00:33:55,021 --> 00:33:57,394
It was still some distance away.

440
00:33:57,762 --> 00:34:00,324
And the person found out the description to be accurate

441
00:34:00,651 --> 00:34:05,222
and that they did lose a camel and they found it because they heard the voice coming from the sky

442
00:34:05,555 --> 00:34:08,717
and also that they missed some of their water.

443
00:34:10,366 --> 00:34:15,091
And these are all signs that were given to them but that wasn't sufficient for them to belief.

444
00:34:15,896 --> 00:34:25,224
Now the story of Al-Israa wal Miraj(ألإسراء ولمعراج) was so difficult for some to handle.

445
00:34:26,256 --> 00:34:30,283
It caused some of the weak Muslims to apostate,

446
00:34:31,519 --> 00:34:33,797
it was such a difficult thing for them to grasp.

447
00:34:34,149 --> 00:34:40,846
But that is the case with these amazing miracles that Allahسبحانه وتعالى would show, His Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

448
00:34:44,119 --> 00:34:47,571
LESSONS TO BE LEARNED FROM AL-ISRAA WAL MIRAJ(ألإسراء ولمعراج).

449
00:34:48,415 --> 00:34:49,497
Number one,

450
00:34:49,788 --> 00:34:55,997
the event of opening the chest of Muhammadﷺ has occurred more than once.

451
00:34:57,040 --> 00:35:01,870
It occurred once when he was with Halima Sadia(حليمه سعديه), when he was a child.

452
00:35:02,147 --> 00:35:07,623
And it occurred another time in the journey of Al-Israa wal Miraj(ألإسراء ولمعراج)

453
00:35:08,026 --> 00:35:12,288
by the way, the meaning of Al- Israa wal Miraj(ألإسراء ولمعراج) is Israa(اِسرَاء) means, traveling at night.

454
00:35:13,323 --> 00:35:15,702
The meaning of Miraj(معراج) is ascending,

455
00:35:16,515 --> 00:35:19,896
Israa(اِسرَاء) is traveling at night, Miraj(معراج) is ascending,

456
00:35:20,211 --> 00:35:23,639
Israa(اِسرَاء) is the journey of Rasool Allah ﷺ from Makkah to Jerusalem.

457
00:35:23,949 --> 00:35:27,105
Al-Miraj(المعراج) is the journey from Jerusalem to the heavens.

458
00:35:27,896 --> 00:35:32,504
So, the event of opening the chest of Rasool Allah ﷺ happened more than once.

459
00:35:32,940 --> 00:35:38,936
And these are two incidents, when it happened and it could have happened another time,

460
00:35:39,507 --> 00:35:43,936
or more than once, in addition to these two occurrences.

461
00:35:45,190 --> 00:35:50,925
Number two, the conversation of Rasool Allah ﷺ with Musaعليه السّلام,

462
00:35:51,124 --> 00:35:56,396
when Allahسبحانه وتعالى prescribed 50 daily prayers on Muhammadﷺ, Muhammadﷺ accepted it.

463
00:35:57,028 --> 00:35:59,535
But when he went down and met Musaعليه السّلام,

464
00:36:00,603 --> 00:36:03,381
Musa(موسى) told him your nation will not be able to handle it.

465
00:36:04,252 --> 00:36:11,097
So, Musa(موسى) is speaking out of experience and that is the value of experience.

466
00:36:12,407 --> 00:36:17,082
Sometimes knowledge does not suffice, you have to have in addition to knowledge, experience,

467
00:36:17,605 --> 00:36:22,031
Musa(موسى) told Muhammadﷺ, I have more experience than you do in dealing with the people,

468
00:36:22,071 --> 00:36:24,525
you are new in this, I have spent my whole life,

469
00:36:24,750 --> 00:36:26,846
dealing with the most difficult people, Bani Israel(بني إسرائيل),

470
00:36:28,113 --> 00:36:31,247
believe me they won't be able to handle it, go back and ask for reduction.

471
00:36:32,144 --> 00:36:34,516
Musa(موسى) himself learned this,

472
00:36:34,626 --> 00:36:37,131
learn that experience, is different than knowledge.

473
00:36:37,391 --> 00:36:43,761
When Musa(موسى) was meeting with Allahعَزّوجَلّ, when he went to meet with Allah, in the journey of the 40 days.

474
00:36:44,793 --> 00:36:49,699
Allahسبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى) that in your absence your people have worshiped the calf,

475
00:36:50,749 --> 00:36:56,980
وَمَا أَعْجَلَكَ عَنْ قَوْمِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ َ

476
00:36:57,365 --> 00:37:04,762
 قَالَ هُمْ أُولَاءِ عَلَىٰ أَثَرِي وَعَجِلْتُ إِلَيْكَ رَبِّ لِتَرْضَىٰ َ

477
00:37:05,413 --> 00:37:14,382
 قَالَ فَإِنَّا قَدْ فَتَنَّا قَوْمَكَ مِنْ بَعْدِكَ وَأَضَلَّهُمُ السَّامِرِيُّ۝

478
00:37:14,871 --> 00:37:18,906
Allahسبحانه وتعالى said that your people have went astray,

479
00:37:19,930 --> 00:37:22,665
and they deviated due to the Samry(سامري),

480
00:37:23,213 --> 00:37:25,515
and he made for them a calf out of gold.

481
00:37:25,697 --> 00:37:28,824
So, Allah told Musaعليه السّلام everything that happened.

482
00:37:29,737 --> 00:37:34,709
Musa(موسى) just received from Allah the 10 tablets, right, 10 tablets, Alal-Alwaah(على الوح).

483
00:37:35,256 --> 00:37:41,758
So, Musa(موسى) had the tablets in his hand, and he was told by Allah that your people have deviated.

484
00:37:42,889 --> 00:37:45,932
So, Musa(موسى) already knew, when Musa(موسى) went back

485
00:37:46,617 --> 00:37:49,440
and he saw his people worshipping the calf.

486
00:37:51,255 --> 00:37:52,396
What did Musa(موسى) do?

487
00:37:52,952 --> 00:37:54,944
He threw the tablets from his hand.

488
00:37:55,977 --> 00:38:02,926
Musaعليه السّلام already knew that how come his response was different when he saw it, compared to when he heard it.

489
00:38:03,601 --> 00:38:05,863
Because seeing something is not like hearing it.

490
00:38:07,113 --> 00:38:12,496
When Allah told him, that your people have deviated, Musa(موسى) had the tablets in his hands and nothing happened.

491
00:38:13,122 --> 00:38:16,789
But when he saw it, with his own eyes, he threw the tablets, it was a surprise for him.

492
00:38:17,532 --> 00:38:19,142
لَيْسَ الْخَبَرْ كَالمُعَايْنَه

493
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:21,186
When you see something is different than hearing it.

494
00:38:22,168 --> 00:38:26,768
Musaعليه السّلام is telling Muhammadﷺ that I have dealt with the people, I have firsthand knowledge,

495
00:38:27,414 --> 00:38:29,617
your people cannot handle this, it's too much.

496
00:38:31,046 --> 00:38:32,763
And he kept on asking for reduction.

497
00:38:33,150 --> 00:38:39,742
And when it was reduced to five, Musa عليه السّلا told Muhammadﷺ even five is too much for them.

498
00:38:41,178 --> 00:38:42,686
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Musa(موسى) was right.

499
00:38:44,377 --> 00:38:45,869
Musa عليه السّلام was right.

500
00:38:46,043 --> 00:38:49,131
How many Muslims don't even pray the five daily prayers.?

501
00:38:50,888 --> 00:38:54,779
How many of them laps and they would pray some and Miss others.

502
00:38:56,366 --> 00:39:01,929
But May Allah reward Musa(موسى) for making it easy on us at least it was reduced to five,

503
00:39:02,262 --> 00:39:05,843
 if it would have been 50 imagine how difficult it would have been.

504
00:39:06,726 --> 00:39:08,078
We're barely doing the five,

505
00:39:09,288 --> 00:39:11,875
what would be the situation?

506
00:39:12,609 --> 00:39:13,926
If we had to do 50,

507
00:39:14,362 --> 00:39:16,262
so we owe it to Musaعليه السّلام

508
00:39:17,312 --> 00:39:20,276
and we need to thank him, immensely for that.

509
00:39:21,915 --> 00:39:26,788
When I said, that the competition between the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) is a compassionate competition.

510
00:39:27,983 --> 00:39:30,064
Musaعليه السّلام even though he wept

511
00:39:31,136 --> 00:39:35,057
when he knew that Muhammadﷺ has a larger following than his.

512
00:39:35,710 --> 00:39:41,903
That didn't make him not giving us his advice, his valuable advice.

513
00:39:42,145 --> 00:39:45,179
So, you can see how eager Musa(موسى) was to help us

514
00:39:46,078 --> 00:39:49,170
and how eager Musa(موسى) was to give his advice to Muhammadﷺ.

515
00:39:49,210 --> 00:39:50,259
So, they loved each other.

516
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:52,026
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) loved each other.

517
00:39:52,273 --> 00:39:55,745
So, their competition was a competition of love of each other

518
00:39:56,414 --> 00:40:00,992
Musaعليه السّلام, he kept on insisting and telling Muhammadﷺ go back and ask for reduction.

519
00:40:02,143 --> 00:40:06,286
And when Musa(موسى) said that, he has more people entering Jannah(جنة) compared to me,

520
00:40:06,500 --> 00:40:09,535
I think we already touched upon the visions

521
00:40:09,575 --> 00:40:14,141
 that Rasool Allah ﷺ had, on the Day of Judgment seeing the different nations of the prophets.

522
00:40:14,799 --> 00:40:17,611
Some prophets have 10 followers, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

523
00:40:17,979 --> 00:40:21,436
Some have five followers, I've seen a prophet with two followers.

524
00:40:21,575 --> 00:40:23,613
 I've seen a prophet with one follower,

525
00:40:23,968 --> 00:40:27,665
and I've seen prophets with no followers at all.

526
00:40:28,551 --> 00:40:31,118
Imagine a prophet coming on the Day of Judgment alone.

527
00:40:31,952 --> 00:40:35,335
They spend their whole life in Da'wah(دعوة) no one responded, nobody

528
00:40:36,417 --> 00:40:39,882
and then when he saw a huge nation, he thought that it is his following,

529
00:40:40,140 --> 00:40:42,238
but then it turned out to be the following of Musa(موسى).

530
00:40:42,278 --> 00:40:46,111
So, that's the greatest Ummah(امة) after the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

531
00:40:47,093 --> 00:40:49,722
The third lesson, the importance of Salah(صلاة),

532
00:40:51,627 --> 00:41:03,859
there is no command, none, whatsoever that was prescribed on us in heavens, except Salah(صلاة).

533
00:41:05,009 --> 00:41:09,693
Every other Ibadah(عبادة), every other ritual that we have was prescribed on the earth.

534
00:41:10,125 --> 00:41:16,438
Jibreel(جبريل) would reveal to Muhammadﷺ, the revelation on Earth with the exception of Salah(صلاة)

535
00:41:16,962 --> 00:41:24,767
it was reserved to be given to Muhammadﷺ in this special one to one meeting between Allah and Muhammadﷺ.

536
00:41:25,870 --> 00:41:32,397
Salah(صلاة) is so important that Allahسبحانه وتعالى prescribed it in a direct conversation

537
00:41:32,437 --> 00:41:36,897
between Him and His Messenger Muhammadﷺ, without anyone in between.

538
00:41:37,676 --> 00:41:42,039
Everything else was a revelation through Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), with the exception of Salah(صلاة),

539
00:41:42,676 --> 00:41:45,753
that just to show you how important Salah(صلاة) is.

540
00:41:46,991 --> 00:41:53,224
Not only to Muhammadﷺ, even when Allah prescribed Salah(صلاة) on the people of Banni Israel(بني إسرائيل),

541
00:41:53,581 --> 00:41:56,255
Allahسبحانه وتعالى prescribed Salah(صلاة) on Musa(موسى)

542
00:41:56,295 --> 00:41:59,870
in the direct conversation that happened between Allah and Musa(موسى) in At-Toor(ألطور),

543
00:42:00,663 --> 00:42:02,266
in the Ayaat in Surat Ta'ha(سورة طه)

544
00:42:02,823 --> 00:42:15,388
إِنَّنِي أَنَا اللَّهُ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا أَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِي وَأَقِمِ الصَّلَاةَ لِذِكْرِي۝

545
00:42:16,245 --> 00:42:18,716
I am Allah, there is no god besides Me.

546
00:42:18,954 --> 00:42:21,200
so establish prayer in my remembrance.

547
00:42:21,934 --> 00:42:24,845
And that was the moment in which Musa(موسى) became a prophet.

548
00:42:25,544 --> 00:42:27,805
So, he was given the commands of prayer,

549
00:42:28,337 --> 00:42:30,377
immediately when he became a prophet.

550
00:42:31,857 --> 00:42:32,691
He was told first,

551
00:42:32,731 --> 00:42:33,756
 لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

552
00:42:33,796 --> 00:42:35,378
and then second, to pray.

553
00:42:35,866 --> 00:42:39,435
And that was when Musa(موسى) was at the age of 40, and he received the revelation from Allah,

554
00:42:39,601 --> 00:42:40,908
when Allah spoke to him directly.

555
00:42:41,207 --> 00:42:42,859
So, that's the value of Salah(صلاة)

556
00:42:43,150 --> 00:42:48,207
Salah(صلاة) is the Ibadah(عبادة), in which Rasool Allahﷺ said: If the Muslim doesn't do it, they have left Islam.

557
00:42:49,403 --> 00:42:52,234
بَيْنَ الْعَبْدْ وَالْكُفْرِ وَ الشِرْكِ تَرْكُ الصَّلَاةْ

558
00:42:52,913 --> 00:43:00,571
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Between a person and becoming a disbeliever is discontinuing prayers, not praying.

559
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:04,912
So, that's how important Salah(صلاة) is

560
00:43:05,164 --> 00:43:13,594
not only is praying important, but even playing around with the time and not praying within the interval of time is a major sin.

561
00:43:13,968 --> 00:43:15,087
The Ayah(آية) that says;

562
00:43:15,522 --> 00:43:26,349
فَخَلَفَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ أَضَاعُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَاتَّبَعُوا الشَّهَوَاتِ ۖ فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا۝

563
00:43:27,279 --> 00:43:29,272
Allahسبحانه وتعالى promised Hellfire to who.?

564
00:43:29,989 --> 00:43:32,945
To the ones, who have lost their prayers.

565
00:43:33,279 --> 00:43:35,506
Ibn Masood(ابن مسعود) gives an interpretation to this Ayah(آية).

566
00:43:35,546 --> 00:43:38,147
He says losing their prayer does not mean that they don't pray,

567
00:43:38,377 --> 00:43:40,163
but it means, they pray past time.

568
00:43:42,321 --> 00:43:45,160
 It is the opinion of Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه

569
00:43:45,443 --> 00:43:49,252
that if a person misses one prayer intentionally without an excuse,

570
00:43:49,585 --> 00:43:51,103
they have left the folds of Islam.

571
00:43:53,539 --> 00:44:01,236
Obviously the scholars have two opinions in regard to the Ahadith(احاديث) that state the disbelief of the one who doesn't pray.

572
00:44:01,675 --> 00:44:07,279
But the end result is that prayer is the most important ritual in Islam.

573
00:44:07,644 --> 00:44:10,958
It is the one thing no one is excused from.

574
00:44:11,470 --> 00:44:16,925
If you don't have enough money, if you don't have the ability to make Hajj(حَجْ), you're excused.

575
00:44:17,752 --> 00:44:19,484
If you are unable to fast,

576
00:44:19,876 --> 00:44:23,538
because of old age or illness, you are excused.

577
00:44:24,176 --> 00:44:28,793
If you don't have wealth, you do not have to pay Zaka'h(زكوة).

578
00:44:29,367 --> 00:44:33,326
But there is no situation, where a person is excused from prayer.

579
00:44:34,139 --> 00:44:36,247
If you can't pray standing up, pray sitting down

580
00:44:36,631 --> 00:44:39,035
you can't pray sitting down, then you pray laying down.

581
00:44:39,491 --> 00:44:43,168
You can't pray laying down because you are paralyzed or something, with your finger.

582
00:44:43,577 --> 00:44:45,907
You can't do with your finger, with your eyes.

583
00:44:46,712 --> 00:44:49,707
But there is no situation where a person is excused from praying.

584
00:44:50,120 --> 00:44:55,737
Even when the battle is going on Salah(صلاة) still has to be done.

585
00:44:56,775 --> 00:44:58,266
In the Ayaat(آيات) of Salat-Ul-Khauf(صلاة الخوف).

586
00:44:59,437 --> 00:45:03,929
So, Salah(صلاة) is the only Ibadah(عبادة) in Islam where there is no excuse of not doing it.

587
00:45:04,665 --> 00:45:07,107
There is no relief of it, it has to be done.

588
00:45:07,529 --> 00:45:13,714
The scholars have said that the Muslim who is spying on the enemy and cannot pray.

589
00:45:13,843 --> 00:45:17,970
This is our classical scholars, they said; such a person can pray with their finger.

590
00:45:19,173 --> 00:45:22,737
But they have to pray. Salah(صلاة) needs to be done.

591
00:45:24,174 --> 00:45:25,184
Number four,

592
00:45:25,700 --> 00:45:34,613
this journey reveals to us the importance of the Holy Land, Jerusalem and its surroundings.

593
00:45:35,285 --> 00:45:39,412
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says; Surat-Ul-Isra'a(سورة الإسراء):

594
00:45:40,273 --> 00:45:55,710
سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى الَّذِي بَارَكْنَا حَوْلَهُ لِنُرِيَهُ مِنْ آيَاتِنَا ۚ

595
00:45:56,535 --> 00:46:01,757
إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ۝

596
00:46:03,383 --> 00:46:09,950
Exalted is He, Who took His servant by night, from Al-Masjid-Ul-Haraam(مسجدالحرام) in Makkah

597
00:46:10,466 --> 00:46:13,388
to Al-Masjid-El-Aqsaa(مسجدالاقصى), the furthest mosque in Jerusalem,

598
00:46:13,923 --> 00:46:15,731
whose surroundings We have blessed.

599
00:46:15,821 --> 00:46:20,888
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says that that's a blessed land to show him of Our signs.

600
00:46:21,592 --> 00:46:24,563
Allah has shown Muhammadﷺ many signs on this journey,

601
00:46:25,657 --> 00:46:27,363
He is the hearing, the seeing.

602
00:46:28,410 --> 00:46:32,555
Jerusalem was promised to the believers,

603
00:46:34,266 --> 00:46:42,597
Ibrahimعليه السّلام was given that promise that your descendants, the believers among them,

604
00:46:43,231 --> 00:46:47,430
will be the guardians of Jerusalem, the Holy Land.

605
00:46:47,966 --> 00:46:55,145
And that was the promise that was fulfilled through the prophets of the children of Israel.

606
00:46:56,133 --> 00:46:59,340
Allahسبحانه وتعالى also promised Jerusalem to Musaعليه السّلام,

607
00:46:59,856 --> 00:47:06,823
now even though Musaعليه السّلام, Moses did not see the result of that promise in his lifetime,

608
00:47:06,863 --> 00:47:10,076
but it occurred in the lifetime of his successor,

609
00:47:10,318 --> 00:47:12,473
Yousha Bin Noon(يوشى بن نون), the Prophet Joshua.

610
00:47:13,022 --> 00:47:16,606
And the children of Israel remained in that land,

611
00:47:17,009 --> 00:47:19,482
as long as they were the bearers of truth.

612
00:47:20,870 --> 00:47:25,539
And when they deviated from the true message of Allah and they fought the prophets

613
00:47:25,658 --> 00:47:29,431
and they attempted to kill Jesus عليه السّلام and they killed other prophets,

614
00:47:29,994 --> 00:47:35,994
Allahسبحانه وتعالى stripped away the land from them, and gave it to the other branch, the descendants of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل).

615
00:47:36,940 --> 00:47:41,543
Allahسبحانه وتعالى gave that to Muhammadﷺ and his Ummah(امة)

616
00:47:41,686 --> 00:47:45,686
because now there are the ones, who are carrying the torch of truth.

617
00:47:46,652 --> 00:47:49,080
So, that land is promised to the believers.

618
00:47:49,813 --> 00:47:54,808
And since now the torch is being carried by the seal of the prophets, Muhammadﷺ,

619
00:47:55,224 --> 00:48:00,279
even though Muhammadﷺ will not open Jerusalem in his lifetime, but he must visit it.

620
00:48:01,002 --> 00:48:02,691
He must go and receive the keys.

621
00:48:04,337 --> 00:48:09,522
And the symbolism in this journey of Rasool Allah ﷺ going to the Masjid(مسجد)

622
00:48:09,816 --> 00:48:12,694
and leading the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) in a prayer

623
00:48:12,964 --> 00:48:18,032
is to show that now Muhammadﷺ is the inheritor of the message of the prophets

624
00:48:18,339 --> 00:48:20,437
and he is a leader on the sons of Adam(آدم).

625
00:48:21,144 --> 00:48:28,118
And the land that was under the custodianship of the prophets of Banni Israel(بني اسرائيل)

626
00:48:28,245 --> 00:48:32,841
is now transferred to the followers of Muhammadﷺ.

627
00:48:33,981 --> 00:48:39,284
And just as Musa(موسى) did not see it in his lifetime, but it happens in the lifetime of his successor Joshua.

628
00:48:39,641 --> 00:48:41,758
Muhammadﷺ did not see it in his lifetime.

629
00:48:41,798 --> 00:48:44,581
And it happened in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه.

630
00:48:44,859 --> 00:48:48,947
The man, whom Rasool Allah ﷺ said; If there's a prophet after me, it would be Umar(عُمَر).

631
00:48:50,692 --> 00:48:54,150
So, that was a blessing that Allah reserved for Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

632
00:48:55,125 --> 00:49:02,039
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), look at the divine destiny, when the Muslims reached to the Gates of Jerusalem

633
00:49:03,079 --> 00:49:11,624
even though, the religious and political leadership of Jerusalem couldnot fight the Muslims and they had to give it up.

634
00:49:12,279 --> 00:49:14,827
They said, We will surrender.

635
00:49:15,037 --> 00:49:19,962
But we cannot surrender to anyone but the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims,

636
00:49:20,559 --> 00:49:24,148
he must come here and take the keys with his own hand.

637
00:49:25,935 --> 00:49:26,865
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

638
00:49:26,905 --> 00:49:31,243
that brought out Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) to travel all the way from Madina to Jerusalem,

639
00:49:31,305 --> 00:49:36,808
because he is the one, who will receive the keys of Jerusalem.

640
00:49:37,244 --> 00:49:43,334
And he went all the way there and he was the one who was given the keys, to the Holy city.

641
00:49:44,625 --> 00:49:53,898
So, now the Muslims are the ones, who have the promise of Allah, the promise of the Holy Land, Bait-Ul-Muqaddas(بيت المقدس).

642
00:49:55,049 --> 00:49:56,224
Number five,

643
00:49:57,791 --> 00:49:58,658
which we mentioned

644
00:49:58,698 --> 00:49:59,783
فَإِنَّ مَعَ الْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا

645
00:50:00,395 --> 00:50:01,736
With difficulty comes ease.

646
00:50:01,776 --> 00:50:07,495
Rasool Allah ﷺ went through some very difficult moments in the 10th year of His revelation.

647
00:50:07,813 --> 00:50:14,241
So, Allahسبحانه وتعالى gave him this blessing, the journey of Isra'a-Wal-Miraj(ألإسراء ولمعراج)

648
00:50:14,479 --> 00:50:19,551
 and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), this was such a treat for Muhammadﷺ.

649
00:50:20,087 --> 00:50:29,913
I mean, there is no tourist journey with so many attractions, as this journey of Isra'a-Wal-Miraj(ألإسراء ولمعراج)

650
00:50:30,731 --> 00:50:35,321
 and to have Jibreel عليه السّلام as your guide, to take you through,

651
00:50:35,616 --> 00:50:38,875
and to meet with the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah

652
00:50:39,320 --> 00:50:47,286
and to go in this journey to the real Wonderland from one place to another and then you enter into paradise, Jannah(جنة).

653
00:50:48,238 --> 00:50:53,541
Rasool Allah ﷺ in that journey, he entered into Jannah(جنة) and he saw the river of Al-Kausar(الكوثر), which was given to him.

654
00:50:54,196 --> 00:50:58,058
Jibreelعليه السّلام told Muhammadﷺ, this is your river, Al-Kausar(ألكوثر).

655
00:50:59,041 --> 00:51:03,192
So, it's also such a bounty that Allahسبحانه وتعالى has given Muhammadﷺ

656
00:51:03,375 --> 00:51:10,382
and that would bring back what we mentioned earlier that you never know what Allahسبحانه وتعالى is hiding for you.

657
00:51:10,975 --> 00:51:14,732
Hajar عليها السّلام we mentioned that when she was running between As-Safa-Wal-Marwa(ألصفاء ولمروة),

658
00:51:14,857 --> 00:51:16,754
she didn't know, she was crying at the time,

659
00:51:16,794 --> 00:51:22,540
she didn't know that this would be followed by the greatest nation the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

660
00:51:23,326 --> 00:51:27,525
So, when you're going through difficulties in this world, you don't know what Allah is reserving for you.

661
00:51:28,503 --> 00:51:29,642
When Allahسبحانه وتعالى says;

662
00:51:29,682 --> 00:51:30,769
فَإِنَّ مَعَ الْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا

663
00:51:30,840 --> 00:51:33,100
With difficulty comes ease, believe in that promise,

664
00:51:33,705 --> 00:51:38,919
with every difficulty, you go through Allahسبحانه وتعالى is reserving for you something.

665
00:51:39,499 --> 00:51:42,790
Whether you get it in this world or the afterlife, you're going to get it.

666
00:51:44,576 --> 00:51:45,908
So, the Muslim should never give up,

667
00:51:46,706 --> 00:51:48,448
should never feel despair.

668
00:51:49,890 --> 00:51:56,766
The sixth lesson the position of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

669
00:51:57,265 --> 00:52:00,367
How did Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) received the news of Al-Israa-Wal-Miraj(ألإسراء ولمعراج).

670
00:52:02,311 --> 00:52:06,924
When the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), were joking around laughing, clapping, whistling,

671
00:52:07,618 --> 00:52:08,884
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was not present

672
00:52:08,924 --> 00:52:12,299
and he was coming into Makkah and someone went and told him. Do you know what happened?

673
00:52:12,659 --> 00:52:16,490
Muhammadﷺ claims that, he went to Jerusalem and he made it back.

674
00:52:17,737 --> 00:52:20,719
Now, what do you think the response of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was?

675
00:52:21,604 --> 00:52:24,186
Well, he did believe but what did he say?

676
00:52:25,435 --> 00:52:27,092
That's an important thing to add.

677
00:52:27,755 --> 00:52:32,618
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: If he said it, then it's the truth.

678
00:52:34,186 --> 00:52:37,682
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did not just accept the information that was given to him.

679
00:52:37,770 --> 00:52:41,135
He said, If he said it, it is the truth.

680
00:52:41,444 --> 00:52:44,266
there's two things to learn from the first segment, if he said it,

681
00:52:45,010 --> 00:52:48,643
and that is the science of verifying Hadith(حديث),

682
00:52:50,424 --> 00:52:53,913
when our scholars study the lives of the narrator's of the Hadith(حديث),

683
00:52:53,977 --> 00:52:57,896
they want to discern whether Muhammadﷺ said it or not,

684
00:52:58,323 --> 00:53:02,846
you were not just going to accept anything that is said, by anyone out there.

685
00:53:03,573 --> 00:53:07,429
We want to make sure that Muhammadﷺ did say it.

686
00:53:08,088 --> 00:53:11,786
And that is, what makes a difference between us and the people of the book

687
00:53:12,128 --> 00:53:17,012
the people of the book, have accepted pretty much everything that came down, to them,

688
00:53:17,710 --> 00:53:21,556
 even if it was separated from the original source by a few centuries.

689
00:53:22,115 --> 00:53:25,847
So, it is a blind faith, it is following Zhan(ظن), conjuncture.

690
00:53:26,244 --> 00:53:30,807
But with the Muslims, no, they had the science of verification

691
00:53:32,247 --> 00:53:36,314
where they studied the lives of thousands and thousands of men and women

692
00:53:37,484 --> 00:53:40,876
to look at their profile whether these are truthful person, people or not,

693
00:53:41,289 --> 00:53:43,749
whether we can accept, what they convey or not.

694
00:53:43,868 --> 00:53:48,813
So, when people go back to Islamic sources, they can feel at ease

695
00:53:49,613 --> 00:53:53,162
that they are dealing with material that has been verified.

696
00:53:54,690 --> 00:53:56,897
اِنْ كَانَ قَالَهَا فَقَدْ صَدَقَ

697
00:53:56,977 --> 00:53:59,299
If he said it, then it is the truth.

698
00:53:59,753 --> 00:54:01,947
So, that is the science of verifying Hadith(حديث).

699
00:54:02,403 --> 00:54:05,185
The second part is, then it is the truth.

700
00:54:05,761 --> 00:54:12,927
And this is the characteristic of Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه

701
00:54:12,967 --> 00:54:16,680
and that's why, he was called As-Siddique(اَلصَّدِيق), the believer.

702
00:54:17,257 --> 00:54:21,132
Whatever Rasool Allah ﷺ says; I will believe him.

703
00:54:22,103 --> 00:54:25,541
I have faith in him, I have faith in everything that he says.

704
00:54:26,751 --> 00:54:29,629
Finally, it's terminology issue.

705
00:54:30,949 --> 00:54:37,638
When we use the word heavens or heaven, it confuses some to think that we are referring to paradise.

706
00:54:38,551 --> 00:54:44,890
Now that's a problem with the English language that these are synonymous heaven and paradise.

707
00:54:45,589 --> 00:54:48,083
But in Islamic terminology, they're not.

708
00:54:48,723 --> 00:54:51,309
Heaven is talking about the sky above us.

709
00:54:51,805 --> 00:54:55,905
That is part of the temporary world that will be destroyed on the Day of Judgment.

710
00:54:56,024 --> 00:54:57,920
Paradise is referring to Jannah(جنة),

711
00:54:58,812 --> 00:55:02,820
Jannah(جنة) is the permanent place of abode for the believers.

712
00:55:03,316 --> 00:55:09,985
So, whenever I'm using the word Heaven, I am not referring to paradise, I'm referring to the sky above us.

713
00:55:12,582 --> 00:55:15,201
I will use as a translation Jannah(جنة), paradise.

714
00:55:15,264 --> 00:55:19,296
So, I hope this confusion is not in the mind of any one of you.

715
00:55:19,336 --> 00:55:21,580
Because I mentioned that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are in the different Heaven.

716
00:55:21,620 --> 00:55:26,160
This is not talking about paradise, it's talking about meetings that occurred with the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

717
00:55:26,525 --> 00:55:30,721
in the heavens above us that are lower than paradise.

718
00:55:31,641 --> 00:55:39,281
Now that Rasool Allah ﷺ has lost the protection of his uncle, Abu Talib(ابو طالب).

719
00:55:40,089 --> 00:55:43,263
And his efforts of Da'wah(دعوة) in Makkah were being blocked.

720
00:55:44,038 --> 00:55:47,172
He tried to search for other alternatives.

721
00:55:48,403 --> 00:55:51,579
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ made a journey to At-Taef(ألطائف).

722
00:55:52,292 --> 00:55:57,076
And he accompanied with him, Zaid Bin Harissaرضي الله عنه.

723
00:55:58,346 --> 00:56:00,101
They went to At-Taef(ألطائف)

724
00:56:00,777 --> 00:56:05,937
and Rasool Allah ﷺ went to the leaders of At-Taef(ألطائف),

725
00:56:06,072 --> 00:56:09,493
Rasool Allah ﷺ, that's his method, he would go to the leaders of the community,

726
00:56:10,437 --> 00:56:12,287
He would enter the house from the gate.

727
00:56:14,112 --> 00:56:18,177
He went to meet the leaders of At-Taef(ألطائف), the tribe of Thaqeef(ثقيف).

728
00:56:18,740 --> 00:56:20,509
And these were three brothers

729
00:56:21,314 --> 00:56:26,357
He presented the message to them and asked them for support and help.

730
00:56:27,566 --> 00:56:31,513
Now these three men responded in a miserable way.

731
00:56:32,092 --> 00:56:33,248
The first one of them said;

732
00:56:33,280 --> 00:56:37,537
اَنَا اَمْرُط كِسَاَء الْكَعْبَهْ اِنْ كَانَ الله قَدْ اَرْسَلَكْ

733
00:56:37,985 --> 00:56:43,642
I'm going to tear apart the clothing of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), if Allah has sent you as a prophet.

734
00:56:44,473 --> 00:56:47,382
The clothing of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) was sacred to them.

735
00:56:48,032 --> 00:56:50,110
So, he is saying that I'm going to tear it apart

736
00:56:51,191 --> 00:56:52,934
if Allah has sent you as a prophet.

737
00:56:55,005 --> 00:57:02,563
The second among them said, his statement was, did not God find anyone better than you to send?

738
00:57:02,839 --> 00:57:05,340
I mean, Isn't there anybody out there better than you?

739
00:57:06,743 --> 00:57:09,899
And the third one said, I cannot speak to you.

740
00:57:10,685 --> 00:57:16,433
 I just can't speak to you, because if you are a messenger from Allah, as you claim,

741
00:57:17,029 --> 00:57:19,627
then you are such an important person.

742
00:57:19,957 --> 00:57:22,120
And I don't think that I'm qualified to speak to you.

743
00:57:23,325 --> 00:57:29,833
And if Allah has not sent you as a messenger, and you are lying, then it's not appropriate for me to speak to a liar.

744
00:57:31,719 --> 00:57:35,299
When Rasool Allah ﷺ, heard their response, he said;

745
00:57:35,339 --> 00:57:39,022
Well, if you don't want to accept my message, at least

746
00:57:40,074 --> 00:57:44,485
keep this conversation that we had, secret, keep it private.

747
00:57:45,354 --> 00:57:51,786
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want the news to reach to Makkah that he has been turned down by the people of Thaqeef(ثقيف),

748
00:57:52,285 --> 00:57:59,550
because it will only add to the persecution of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), towards the Muslims.

749
00:57:59,997 --> 00:58:01,359
So, he said keep it private

750
00:58:01,978 --> 00:58:05,484
but they were such evil men and rude.

751
00:58:05,545 --> 00:58:10,593
What they did is, they went to the fools among them and their slaves and their servants

752
00:58:10,926 --> 00:58:17,141
and they asked them to go and revile Muhammadﷺ and scream at him and

753
00:58:17,554 --> 00:58:25,017
imagine these crowds surrounding Muhammadﷺ, pelting Muhammadﷺ and Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), with rocks,

754
00:58:25,344 --> 00:58:28,319
screaming at them yelling, chasing them away.

755
00:58:28,541 --> 00:58:32,149
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) had to run out of At-Taef(ألطائف).

756
00:58:32,690 --> 00:58:36,245
And Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), he was protecting the body of Muhammadﷺ,

757
00:58:36,285 --> 00:58:39,607
shielding him from the rocks that the people of Thaqeef(ثقيف) are throwing.

758
00:58:40,920 --> 00:58:47,964
And they took refuge, they took shelter in a farm that belonged to two men from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), Ibn Rabiyyah(ابن ربيعه).

759
00:58:48,827 --> 00:58:55,408
So, they went into this farm and they finally got away from the fools of the Thaqeef(ثقيف)

760
00:58:56,754 --> 00:59:00,452
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was exhausted

761
00:59:01,360 --> 00:59:02,709
his feet were bleeding.

762
00:59:03,869 --> 00:59:08,035
And he was hurt because of the way he was treated by the people of Thaqeef (ثقيف).

763
00:59:09,662 --> 00:59:15,920
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Allahسبحانه تعالى sent down help on Muhammadﷺ, he was very hungry at that time.

764
00:59:16,244 --> 00:59:19,300
The two owners of the farm who belong to Makkah.

765
00:59:19,761 --> 00:59:25,887
They told their servant Addaas(عداس), who was a Christian.

766
00:59:27,111 --> 00:59:31,066
They told him go and take some grapes and give it to Muhammadﷺ,

767
00:59:31,106 --> 00:59:37,076
they felt sympathy for Muhammadﷺ, even though they were two of his staunch enemies

768
00:59:37,869 --> 00:59:42,112
but now when they are in a foreign land in different territory,

769
00:59:42,509 --> 00:59:49,234
they felt sympathy towards Muhammadﷺ, they decided that we should stand up for our tribesman,

770
00:59:50,102 --> 00:59:51,936
we should stand up for Muhammadﷺ.

771
00:59:51,996 --> 00:59:54,295
So, at least let's give him these grapes.

772
00:59:54,335 --> 00:59:58,715
So they sent Addaas(عداس) and they told him take this plate of grapes and give it to Muhammadﷺ.

773
00:59:59,437 --> 01:00:04,043
Addaas(عداس), he carried the grapes and he went to Muhammadﷺ and he presented it to him.

774
01:00:05,504 --> 01:00:09,201
Muhammadﷺ said بسم الله, in the name of Allah and he said it loudly.

775
01:00:10,130 --> 01:00:12,732
Addaas(عداس) was surprised.

776
01:00:14,433 --> 01:00:17,956
And he asked Muhammadﷺ, he said;

777
01:00:18,742 --> 01:00:23,152
These words are not said by people in this land.

778
01:00:24,493 --> 01:00:27,668
Arabs, people in this area don't speak these words.

779
01:00:28,676 --> 01:00:32,912
The Messenger of Allah, from these words of Addaas(عداس)

780
01:00:32,952 --> 01:00:39,359
was able to imply that he's a foreigner and he might be following a different religion.

781
01:00:39,399 --> 01:00:43,589
So, he told Addaas(عداس), where are you from, and what is your religion?

782
01:00:43,966 --> 01:00:47,237
And Rasool Allah ﷺ used to ask any people he would meet, where are you from.?

783
01:00:48,125 --> 01:00:51,749
So, he told Addaas(عداس) where are you from, and what is your religion.?

784
01:00:52,269 --> 01:00:59,134
Addaas(عداس) responded by saying, I am a Christian man from Ninawa(نينوى), Ninawa(نينوى) in Iraq.

785
01:01:00,523 --> 01:01:07,523
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, so you are from the village of the pious man, Younas Ibn Matta(يونس إبن مته),

786
01:01:07,706 --> 01:01:13,134
Johna Son of Imatae, Prophet of Allah.

787
01:01:13,975 --> 01:01:19,761
Addaas(عداس) said; And how do you know about Johna son of Imatae,

788
01:01:20,687 --> 01:01:24,378
Muhammadﷺ said: He is my brother.

789
01:01:25,421 --> 01:01:27,720
He was a prophet and I'm a prophet.

790
01:01:28,668 --> 01:01:35,092
When Addaas(عداس) heard that he immediately bent down and started kissing the feet of Rasool Allah ﷺ

791
01:01:35,132 --> 01:01:37,013
and then he kissed his hands and head.

792
01:01:37,984 --> 01:01:41,761
Now the two owners of the farm, from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

793
01:01:42,263 --> 01:01:47,204
when they saw that they looked at each other and said, Look, he has already corrupted our slave.

794
01:01:48,494 --> 01:01:51,212
Muhammadﷺ would Da'wah(دعوة) wherever he is.

795
01:01:51,252 --> 01:01:55,545
And these two men who felt sympathy towards Muhammadﷺ are now regretting it.

796
01:01:56,230 --> 01:01:59,722
We sent in, our slave to take some fruit to him and he has corrupted our slave.

797
01:02:00,178 --> 01:02:02,313
When Addaas(عداس) came back, they told him What's wrong with you?

798
01:02:02,353 --> 01:02:04,575
How come you were kissing his feet, hands and head?

799
01:02:04,969 --> 01:02:09,908
He said on all Earth, there is no man finer than him.

800
01:02:10,067 --> 01:02:14,176
He told me something that no one other than a prophet can know.

801
01:02:14,829 --> 01:02:19,461
They told him; Don't let this man make you leave your religion

802
01:02:19,827 --> 01:02:21,884
because your religion is better than his.

803
01:02:22,364 --> 01:02:25,159
Now what did the two sons of Rabiya(ربيعة) know about Christianity,

804
01:02:25,679 --> 01:02:32,803
but it is Kuffr(كفر) that is in their heart that will make them say whatever, would deceive the people.

805
01:02:33,810 --> 01:02:36,652
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

